- op: discuss  # 498b
  at: '2026-04-10T21:57:19Z'  # 498b
  by: agent  # 498b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 498b
  clock: 3  # 498b
  nonce: 498b  # 498b
  message: "Facet 1 shipped in PR #2918 (merged). Proposing concrete fix for Facet 2 — requires human approval because it touches .agent/hooks/_shared/stop_logic.sh (governance).\n\n## Proposed change\n\nExtend the jq merge in `.agent/hooks/_shared/stop_logic.sh` at lines 288-294 to set `last_completed_utc` to the current UTC timestamp WHEN the Path 3 (full reflection) guidance file is being generated. This gives `last_completed_utc` a deterministic, hook-maintained writer instead of relying on the agent to manually execute the python snippet in stop_reflect.md.\n\n## Semantic change\n\nToday: `last_completed_utc` means \"time the agent last completed a reflection cycle\" (only settable by the agent).\nAfter: `last_completed_utc` means \"time the stop hook last told the agent to reflect\" (settable by the hook).\n\nBoth semantics serve the same purpose — gating the cooldown-vs-reflection path at ELAPSED_MIN=30. The new semantic is strictly more reliable because:\n- It does not depend on agent discipline (the agent must remember to run a python snippet).\n- It cannot get stuck in a self-referential loop (the hook refreshes the timestamp itself).\n- The cooldown path becomes meaningful again: \"if we told the agent to reflect in the last 30 min, be in cooldown mode\".\n\n## Patch sketch\n\n```bash\n# In stop_logic.sh, lines 288-294 (before Path 3 guidance file generation).\n# Modify the jq merge to also set last_completed_utc when we are about to\n# generate a reflection guidance file (ELAPSED_MIN >= 30).\n\nNOW_UTC=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\n\n# Existing jq merge call, extended:\nif printf '%s' \"$_EXISTING\" | jq \\\n      --arg gf \"$GUIDANCE_FILE\" \\\n      --arg bc \"${BAKEOFF_CONVERGENCE_LINE:-}\" \\\n      --arg bs \"${_SESSION_DIR:-}\" \\\n      --arg bt \"${_SESSION_TYPE:-}\" \\\n      --arg now \"$NOW_UTC\" \\\n      --arg elapsed \"$ELAPSED_MIN\" \\\n      '. + {guidance_file: $gf}\n         + (if $bc != \"\" then {bakeoff_convergence: $bc} else {} end)\n         + (if $bs != \"\" then {bakeoff_session_path: $bs, bakeoff_session_type: $bt} else {} end)\n         + (if ($elapsed | tonumber) >= 30 then {last_completed_utc: $now} else {} end)' \\\n      > \"$TMP\" 2>/dev/null; then\n  mv \"$TMP\" \"$STATE_FILE_FOR_GF\"\nfi\n```\n\nNote: the new condition `if $elapsed >= 30` is the SAME condition that gates Path 3 guidance file generation (line 344). So the timestamp is refreshed exactly when Path 3 fires — semantically aligned with \"we told the agent to reflect\".\n\n## Side effects to verify\n\n1. **Cooldown path (Path 2) becomes live again.** Currently unreachable because ELAPSED_MIN has been stuck at ~15,840 min for 11 days. After this fix, the next hook fire within 30 minutes of a Path 3 reflection will correctly take Path 2. Agents will see `stop_guidance_cooldown_*.md` files again. Test: trigger two stop hook fires 5 min apart; second should generate a cooldown file.\n\n2. **The python snippet in `.agent/stop_reflect.md` lines 85-128 becomes redundant for the `last_completed_utc` field.** Should be deleted from stop_reflect.md to prevent confusion (two writers for the same field). The snippet also writes notes, last_pr, branch, pending_todos — those fields are NOT touched by the hook, so the agent should still update them (but via the shorter snippet in recover-state-playbook.md, not via stop_reflect.md).\n\n3. **`recover-state-playbook.md` jq snippet stays as-is.** It updates only `notes`, which is still the agent's responsibility.\n\n## Governance surface\n\nFiles changed:\n- `.agent/hooks/_shared/stop_logic.sh` — governance, needs human approval\n- `.agent/stop_reflect.md` — governance, needs human approval (remove redundant snippet)\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — not governance\n\nFiles NOT changed:\n- `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/recover-state-playbook.md` — behavior unchanged\n- `AGENTS.md` — behavior unchanged (AGENTS.md already says \"Keep notes fresh after key milestones\" which remains accurate for the notes field)\n\n## Test plan\n\n1. Unit test for stop_logic.sh behavior — add/extend a dry-run test that verifies the STATE_FILE is updated with a fresh `last_completed_utc` when ELAPSED_MIN >= 30.\n2. Integration: manually run the stop hook with STOP_HOOK_DRY_RUN=1, inspect the output, confirm the new field is set.\n3. Manual: wait for the next natural stop hook fire (or trigger one), verify `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/guidance_log/last_stop_check.json` now has today's timestamp.\n\n## Requesting approval\n\n@jgstern — OK to proceed? If yes, I'll branch, make the changes, run pytest, and open a PR. Expected diff size: ~5 lines added to stop_logic.sh, ~40 lines removed from stop_reflect.md, CHANGELOG entry.\n\nIf you want me to also shrink the schema (remove fields the hook can't maintain) or move the deletion of the stop_reflect.md snippet into a follow-up PR, let me know."  # 498b
