- op: discuss  # 3517
  at: '2026-04-10T23:22:12Z'  # 3517
  by: agent  # 3517
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3517
  clock: 11  # 3517
  nonce: '3517'  # 3517
  message: "(previous \"test reply\" entry was me debugging flag ordering; the --ack-thread flag must come BEFORE the item_id, not after, and the CLI gives a misleading error otherwise. Another shape of the weak-enforcement problem — CLI is trusting me to guess ordering. Noting but not filing a separate item yet.)\n\nAcknowledged — proceeding with Option B (split file) + dedicated tool for the notes file.\n\n## Revised design for INV-jofaf facet 2\n\nHook-owned fields go in stop_hook_state.json (single writer: stop_logic.sh). Agent-owned notes go in agent_notes.json (single writer: scripts/agent-notes tool, which only accepts --set/--append/--show and cannot touch other fields).\n\nImplementation order within the PR:\n1. Add scripts/agent-notes tool + unit tests.\n2. Modify stop_logic.sh to write stop_hook_state.json with last_completed_utc as a hook-maintained field. Same jq merge pattern as today, just a new target filename and a new key.\n3. Update setup.py _check_reflection_state (and any other reader) to point at stop_hook_state.json instead of last_stop_check.json.\n4. Update recover-state-playbook.md: reads both files, uses scripts/agent-notes for notes updates, deletes the raw jq snippet.\n5. Delete the python snippet from .agent/stop_reflect.md — or replace with a one-liner that calls scripts/agent-notes.\n6. One-time migration on first stop hook fire: if legacy last_stop_check.json exists, split its fields into the two new files and delete the legacy. Self-healing, no manual step.\n7. CHANGELOG entry.\n\nGovernance files touched: .agent/hooks/_shared/stop_logic.sh, .agent/stop_reflect.md. Needs human review, but the design is approved per this discussion. I will open the PR when ready; you review and merge.\n\n## Audit tool separately filed\n\nFiled as WI-sofop-mafar-jatar-dafik-nikoj-tijad-gasig-tukag (P2). Candidate file patterns: stop_hook_state.json, bakeoff session state.json files, guidance files, tracker item created/updated, ADR frontmatter dates, changelog/pyproject version, lab notebook filenames. Tool walks configured patterns, extracts embedded timestamps via jq/regex, compares to filesystem mtime, reports mismatches above per-file-type threshold. Ordering: INV-jofaf facet 2 first (stabilizes stop_hook_state.json schema), then WI-sofop.\n\n## Current work in flight\n\nPrecursor PR #2923 (INV-forim: 4 linkers that overwrite edge.meta and destroy access_mode/dest_access_mode) is currently in CI. Once it merges, I will run Phase A baseline data collection with REAL polyglot edge coverage — currently the would_admit_dst_reader counter reads 0 on every repo because those edges have no dest_access_mode due to the bug I found during Phase A. Phase B option 2 follows. INV-jofaf facet 2 can slot in before Phase B or after Phase C's decision gate; I'll default to after Phase B PR merges unless you say otherwise."  # 3517
- op: discuss  # 27c5
  at: '2026-04-11T00:40:50Z'  # 27c5
  by: agent  # 27c5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 27c5
  clock: 12  # 27c5
  nonce: 27c5  # 27c5
  message: "PR #2926 is up and CI passed. Governance mode — awaiting your review and merge.\n\nhttps://codeberg.org/iterabloom/hypergumbo/pulls/2926\n\n## Summary of changes\n\nTwo files, one writer each:\n\n- `~/<repo>_lab_notebook/guidance_log/stop_hook_state.json` — written only by `stop_logic.sh`. Contains `last_completed_utc` (now hook-maintained on Path 3 fire, no agent action required), `current_branch` (derived from `git branch --show-current`), `guidance_file`, and the bakeoff fields.\n- `~/<repo>_lab_notebook/guidance_log/agent_notes.json` — written only by new `scripts/agent-notes` CLI. Single `notes` field. Tool accepts `--set`, `--append`, `--show`, `--clear`. Physically cannot touch hook-owned fields by construction.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `scripts/agent-notes` (new, 170 lines, Python) — CLI for the notes file.\n- `.agent/hooks/_shared/stop_logic.sh` (governance) — writes stop_hook_state.json instead of last_stop_check.json, adds `last_completed_utc` auto-refresh on Path 3, adds `current_branch`, self-healing migration on first run, cooldown path reads notes from agent_notes.json with legacy fallback.\n- `.agent/stop_reflect.md` (governance) — removes the 50-line python snippet that manually wrote last_stop_check.json. Replaced with a single `scripts/agent-notes --set` call.\n- `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/recover-state-playbook.md` — describes the new two-file layout and the tool.\n- `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/setup.py` — `_check_reflection_state` reads stop_hook_state.json first, falls back to legacy path during migration window. Accepts `current_branch` or legacy `branch`.\n- `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/tests/test_setup.py` — 2 new tests for new-schema path and missing `current_branch` case. Existing tests exercise the fallback branch unchanged.\n- `CHANGELOG.md`\n\n## Self-healing migration\n\nOn the first hook fire after merge, `stop_logic.sh` detects legacy `last_stop_check.json` and seeds `stop_hook_state.json` (hook-owned fields) + `agent_notes.json` (notes field), then deletes the legacy. No manual migration step.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- All 4259 tests pass, 100% coverage on all changed source files.\n- Smoke-tested `scripts/agent-notes --set/--append/--show/--clear` end-to-end with `AGENT_NOTES_FILE` override.\n\n## Verification after merge\n\n1. On the next stop hook fire, `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/guidance_log/stop_hook_state.json` should appear with `last_completed_utc` set to the current UTC time (matching file mtime), and `last_stop_check.json` should be gone.\n2. `agent_notes.json` should have whatever notes were in the legacy file migrated into it (or an empty object if notes were empty).\n3. `scripts/htrac setup` should pass the reflection_state check (reads the new file).\n\n## Once merged\n\n- I will close INV-jofaf as `satisfied` with positive evidence.\n- Next item on the queue is WI-hukoh Phase C/D follow-up (pending your decision on whether to ship option 2 as dormant or close with ADR amendment) and the WI-sofop audit tool."  # 27c5
- op: discuss  # 2918
  at: '2026-04-11T01:28:45Z'  # 2918
  by: human  # 2918
  actor: jgstern  # 2918
  clock: 13  # 2918
  nonce: '2918'  # 2918
  message: "\"On the first hook fire after merge, `stop_logic.sh` detects legacy `last_stop_check.json` and seeds `stop_hook_state.json` (hook-owned fields) + `agent_notes.json` (notes field), then deletes the legacy. No manual migration step\"\n -- I really *really* do *not* love this. It's like you built a feature for the sole purpose of hiding a defect. If the legacy `last_stop_check.json` exists, we should solve the problem by making it not exist. Not by writing code that will inexplicably re-create the file and additional code to delete said file."  # 2918
